# Power moves to the other guide in lambda / (2 (n_even - n_odd)) = 13.05 um, from the supermodes of the transverse grid.
# Reference: full transfer at that length, half at half of it. Monitors use the modes of the separate guides, which overlap slightly at small gaps.
title Directional coupler, two 0.5 um guides 150 nm apart
window width=14 length=28
guide straight x=-0.325 width=0.5 from=0 to=28
guide straight x=0.325 width=0.5 from=0 to=28
launch mode x=-0.325 width=0.5
monitor half_cross z=6.5 x=0.325 width=0.5
monitor cross_full z=13 x=0.325 width=0.5
monitor bar_full z=13 x=-0.325 width=0.5
monitor bar_end z=28 x=-0.325 width=0.5
monitor cross_end z=28 x=0.325 width=0.5
expect power half_cross 0.495465978 2e-7
expect power cross_full 0.992922740 2e-7
expect power bar_full 0.005341318 2e-7
expect power bar_end 0.948128252 2e-7
expect power cross_end 0.056440567 2e-7
expect neff 2.658815502 2e-8
expect power_above cross_full 0.99
expect power_below bar_full 0.015
expect power half_cross 0.5 0.02
expect sum bar_end cross_end 1.0 0.01
